   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\":[{\"id\":\"T1119\",\"name\":\"Automated Collection\",\"tactics\":[\"Collection\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The alert shows an attempt to access a sensitive file, which is consistent with automated data collection activities that may precede data exfiltration.\"},{\"id\":\"T1083\",\"name\":\"File and Directory Discovery\",\"tactics\":[\"Discovery\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The user (erodriguez) attempted to read a sensitive file at an Administrator path, suggesting reconnaissance to identify valuable files for potential exfiltration.\"},{\"id\":\"T1048\",\"name\":\"Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol\",\"tactics\":[\"Exfiltration\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The alert explicitly indicates a data_exfiltration_prevention block reason, suggesting the system detected an attempt to exfiltrate sensitive data as an alternative to normal data handling channels.\"}],\"identity_signals\":null,\"key_findings\":\"User erodriguez on LAPTOP-JENKINS attempted unauthorized read access to a sensitive Excel file located in the Administrator profile directory. The EDR system's data exfiltration prevention control successfully blocked the access, preventing potential data loss. The suspicious file path and block reason suggest either credential misuse or lateral movement by an attacker attempting to stage sensitive data for exfiltration.\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"severity_rationale\":\"This alert represents suspicious activity originating from an internal host (LAPTOP-JENKINS) targeting sensitive administrative data with a clear exfiltration intent. Although the control blocked the access, the attempt itself to access Administrator-owned sensitive files from a standard user account (erodriguez) indicates either account compromise or privilege escalation. This meets the high-severity threshold as an internal host attempting unauthorized data access with exfiltration indicators.\",\"confidence\":0.78,\"recommended_response\":\"Immediately isolate LAPTOP-JENKINS from the network and initiate a forensic investigation. Verify whether erodriguez's credentials have been compromised by checking recent authentication logs, MFA activity, and other access patterns. Review EDR telemetry for signs of malware, persistence mechanisms, or lateral movement from this host. Interview the user to determine if the access attempt was legitimate. If compromise is confirmed, reset credentials, audit all files accessed by this user in the past 24 hours, and scan for C2 communication or exfiltration staging artifacts.\",\"rounds_used\":0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "diagnostics": null,
