     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.65, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.75, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"The investigation demonstrates solid foundational analysis with strong severity justification and comprehensive response recommendations. However, citation quality needs improvement: T1119 (Automated Collection) is weakly justified since there's no evidence of automation in a single access attempt, and T1048 (Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol) is premature since the access was blocked before any exfiltration occurred. Consider whether these techniques truly apply or if T1552 (Unsecured Credentials) or T1078 (Valid Accounts) might better fit a potential credential misuse scenario. Additionally, the investigation could be more complete by explicitly addressing why a standard user account accessed an Administrator profile directory (legitimate admin task vs. compromise indicator) and whether the sensitive_data.xlsx file is typically accessed by this user, which would significantly impact severity calibration.\"}",
